  "id": "COMPOUND:23161 - PROTEIN:5942",
  "verbalization": "Dichotomine E appears to have a shared target of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Cassialactone and Petroraspailyne B1. These compounds all ultimately lead to Tankyrase-2, suggesting a potential pathway where Dichotomine E may exert its effects through a similar mechanism. The evidence indicates that Microtubule-associated protein 1B is a common intermediate in the targeting of Tankyrase-2, implying that Dichotomine E might act through a related molecular mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of microtubule dynamics or other cellular processes that are modulated by Tankyrase-2. The consistent targeting of Microtubule-associated protein 1B across different compounds supports the idea of a shared biological role, although the exact mechanism by which Dichotomine E influences this pathway remains to be elucidated.",
